  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Mendocino College Physical Therapist Assistant Program Student Handbook 2025-2026, section 1.8 'Program Curriculum' ('an example of the course sequence to complete the requirements for an Associates of Science in Physical Therapist Assisting'). Six semesters: two prerequisite semesters + four PTA program semesters. Semester sums: 16 + 15 + 15 + 15 + 15 + 17 = 93, verified against the handbook's per-semester TOTALs. The handbook states 'Total for associate's degree in PTA 83' with the footnote '**Degree total does not include units for CHM 200 or the 6 doublecounted units for Studies in Culture and Wellness' - i.e., 93 - 4 (CHM 200) - 6 (double-counted Studies in Culture/Wellness) = 83; encoded here at the exact sequenced sum 93 with this documented. Course titles and units are taken from the handbook wholesale (section 1.8 sequence table + 1.9 course descriptions). Known discrepancy: the 2026-2027 catalog COURSES section lists different units for PTA 105L (1.5 vs handbook 1), PTA 106L (0.5 vs handbook 1), and PTA 118 (1 vs handbook 3); the handbook is used wholesale with catalog_year 2025-2026. GE/Institutional choice slots use ANY-MENDOCINO-* codes; the handbook notes GE/Institutional courses 'may be completed prior to entering the program, and in different semesters.' Prerequisite chains per catalog: PTA 118 requires PTA 101, 102, 103, 103L, 104, 104L; PTA 121 (Clinical Practicum 1) requires all pre-Semester-5 PTA courses; PTA 122 (Clinical Practicum 2) requires all pre-Semester-6 PTA courses.",
